      "writtenOn": "2025-11-04T15:09:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this might lead to potentially misleading information.\n\n- The Runnable gets scheduled for async/parallel execution and receives a copy of all currently running operations.\n- The Runnable is long running, by the time some internal timer starts in the unnable all the operations that were copied here have already finished. \n- Yet the timer will have all of them logged as parents",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 85,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "28e421b75489e42be904bd05c83ae87636e8d8c0",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18337393_ceb51db5",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/logging/LoggingContext.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 85,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-05T12:50:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point. I think there are 2 ways to look at this.\n\n1. The currently running operations did schedule/start the async/parallel execution, so it makes sense to show them as the caller that triggered this.\n\n2. Showing the currently running operations as callers gives the wrong impression that the operations that are recorded with internal timers would be sub-steps of these parent operations (which may not be the case).\n\nI think conveying the information about which operation scheduled/started the async/parallel execution (1.) makes sense. To avoid confusion with 2. I\u0027ve now added a timer in LoggingContextAwareRunnable/LoggingContextAwareCallable to record the execution (the call of the run/call method). For this timer we are setting the thread name in a new metadata field, which we use to prefix the operation name when formatting the callers/operations. This way we can see from the caller chain where it does async calls.\n\nExample:\n\u0027Post Review Request\u0027 \u003e \u0027Post Review Op\u0027 \u003e \u0027[EmailSender-97874] Runnable\u0027 \u003e \u0027Send Email\u0027",
      "parentUuid": "70f23c33_5451aef4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 85,
        "endChar": 51
      },
